        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add session-limit reset confetti celebration",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an opt-in **Session limit confetti** celebration that plays full-screen confetti when a provider's semantic session usage resets, alongside the existing weekly-limit celebration.\n\n<img width=\"658\" height=\"854\" alt=\"Session limit confetti preference\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d5c9bb6-7680-436f-bf4a-14efd7b38195\" />\n\nThe setting is **off by default**. Users explicitly enable it under Settings → Advanced → Session limit confetti.\n\n## Maintainer hardening\n\n- Resolve non-Codex session observations through the canonical `sessionQuotaWindow` seam rather than treating every approximately five-hour history lane as a session.\n- Require generic primary windows to carry an explicit short session duration; unknown-duration monthly credit pools cannot trigger session confetti.\n- Resolve Codex through the semantic consumer projection, so session detection is stable when lanes are reordered.\n- Persist the selected source with detector state. A source change establishes a new baseline instead of generating false confetti.\n- Preserve legacy persisted detector state so upgrades can still recognize the first real reset.\n- Ignore incomplete provider samples so a temporarily missing session window cannot become a false reset.\n- Recognize z.ai's semantic five-hour session lane even when weekly and monthly windows occupy the primary and secondary slots.\n- Keep session and weekly detector state independent; existing weekly-limit behavior is unchanged.\n- Add focused coverage for Copilot fallback, arbitrary secondary-window rejection, Antigravity source changes, unknown-duration credits, generic-history rejection, legacy state, Codex lane ordering, detector isolation, incomplete samples, and z.ai lane ordering.\n- Isolate global notification observers by provider account identity so the reset suite remains deterministic under parallel execution.\n- Keep the preference default-off and thank @bystritskiy in the changelog.\n\n## Validation — exact head `87c136e8b`\n\n- `make check` — pass (format, lint, locale, package, signing, and documentation checks).\n- `make test` — pass; 525 selections across 44/44 groups on the post-#1771 rebase.\n- `swift test --filter UsageStorePlanUtilization` — 105 tests across six suites pass, including the unknown-duration credit-pool regression.\n- Structured branch autoreview against current `origin/main` — clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Packaged production app — `codesign --verify --deep --strict` passes; binary UUID `8D90911E-7256-3257-BC54-9CC4CFAAB6BD`; binary SHA-256 `dee0c66548c3cf692df2da0994f8149c4e90f66a3628da6805dcb706d1ca1e4e`.\n- Tart macOS VM (`provider=tart`, lease `cbx_6f2e51df5507`) — exact bundle `/Users/admin/Applications/CodexBar-1775-87c1.app` stayed running as PID 19149; remote signature, UUID, and SHA-256 match the host package; the persisted preference read back enabled and the exact bundle rendered the Advanced setting enabled beside the unchanged weekly option. Local screenshots are intentionally not uploaded by the maintainer.\n- Live full-screen confetti and exact-dSYM panel retention were captured on the preceding confetti-UI-identical head; the later changes only tighten reset-source/state semantics, isolate tests, integrate current main, and extract settings-default loading.\n- [Replacement exact-head CI](https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/actions/runs/28519741660) — approved and running for `87c136e8b`; merge remains blocked until every required check is terminal green.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThe detector posts one session-reset event on a real above-threshold → reset transition from a semantic session lane. The app reuses the existing click-through, full-screen confetti overlay; no new rendering surface or provider probe is introduced.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
